WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.970
Let's make A twig treasure pot.

2
00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.980
Wrap a small reused container in a tidy coat of short twigs.

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.855
The container provides the structure; paper tape holds the decoration.

4
00:00:11.235 --> 00:00:13.315
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:13.695 --> 00:00:16.425
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:16.805 --> 00:00:19.050
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.350
An adult prepares twig lengths and checks edges.

8
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.450
Handle the finished pot by its base; it is decorative, not a food container.

9
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:30.023
Step 1.

10
00:00:30.403 --> 00:00:31.538
Choose the base.

11
00:00:31.918 --> 00:00:35.268
Choose a clean cardboard container with an intact bottom.

12
00:00:35.648 --> 00:00:37.328
Stand it on the table.

13
00:00:37.708 --> 00:00:42.241
Select twigs that reach no higher than its rim so they cannot poke hands

14
00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:42.888
reaching inside.

15
00:00:43.268 --> 00:00:44.648
Grown-up help.

16
00:00:45.028 --> 00:00:48.773
Prepare smooth twigs without asking children to cut them.

17
00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.347
Step 2.

18
00:00:51.727 --> 00:00:53.222
Lay out a twig coat.

19
00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:58.757
Lay two tape strips sticky side up, parallel and about 5 centimetres apart.

20
00:00:59.137 --> 00:01:04.237
Put twigs across both strips, side by side, leaving a small gap between twigs.

21
00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:05.997
Grown-up help.

22
00:01:06.377 --> 00:01:08.677
Keep the tape strips steady if needed.

23
00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.512
Step 3.

24
00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:13.167
Wrap the container.

25
00:01:13.547 --> 00:01:17.590
Lift the twig row by its taped sides and bend it around the outside

26
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:18.457
of the container.

27
00:01:18.837 --> 00:01:21.087
Keep twig ends level with the bottom.

28
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:25.142
Stop where the row meets itself; leave the opening clear.

29
00:01:25.522 --> 00:01:26.902
Grown-up help.

30
00:01:27.282 --> 00:01:29.782
Help hold the container while wrapping.

31
00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.317
Step 4.

32
00:01:32.697 --> 00:01:34.462
Secure the outside.

33
00:01:34.842 --> 00:01:39.051
Wrap one tape strip around the outside near the top and one near the

34
00:01:39.051 --> 00:01:39.352
bottom.

35
00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.947
Overlap tape ends by at least 3 centimetres.

36
00:01:43.327 --> 00:01:47.317
Press every twig gently; add a short tape patch if one moves.

37
00:01:47.697 --> 00:01:49.077
Grown-up help.

38
00:01:49.457 --> 00:01:51.942
Check all pieces are secure before use.

39
00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:54.509
Step 5.

40
00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:56.494
Name your collection.

41
00:01:56.874 --> 00:02:01.269
Add a paper label and choose a few large, clean natural treasures.

42
00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:04.084
Lift the pot by its original base.

43
00:02:04.464 --> 00:02:07.184
Keep it indoors and take out any damp pieces.

44
00:02:07.564 --> 00:02:08.944
Grown-up help.

45
00:02:09.324 --> 00:02:12.644
Check collected treasures are appropriate to handle.

46
00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.082
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

47
00:02:17.462 --> 00:02:21.012
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

48
00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:23.412
Your creation can look different.

49
00:02:23.792 --> 00:02:29.367
Peel off tape, reuse the container, and sort twigs and mixed materials separately.

50
00:02:29.747 --> 00:02:32.787
Store dry indoors and check the twig coat before moving it.

51
00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.157
Well done.

52
00:02:34.537 --> 00:02:36.967
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

